** Files and edits

| Order | Repo             | File                                 | Edit                                                       | Reaches a fresh install by |
|-------+------------------+--------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------|
| 1     | bisos-pip/common | =py3/bisos/common/baseDirBxRepos.py= | =pbdDict_bxReposRoot=: the 10 gitGroups cloned by bisos.common | a bisos.common release     |
| 2     | bisos/bsip4      | =bin/bxRepos-gitist.pcs=             | =reposList=: add =mb-ephemera/base=, =rePublication/base=  | git (bsip4 is cloned)      |

1. *=baseDirBxRepos.py=, =pbdDict_bxReposRoot= only* (its body, outside the dblocks):
   - A local helper beside =gitClone=, e.g.
     =gitGroupDir(locName, srvName, withBase=True, withDotGithub=True)=: =directory(locName)=;
     =gitClone(f"{locName}/base", f"{srvName}/base")=; =gitClone(f"{locName}/.github", f"{srvName}/.github")=;
     and =command(f"{locName}/gitGroup", f"cd {root}/{locName} && ln -sfn .github gitGroup")=.
     The link is made with =command()= because =symLink()= always makes an absolute link
     (=srcFullPathObtain= joins the root), and the model's link is the relative =gitGroup -> .github=.
     =gitClone= already handles a local name that differs from the server's (=blee= <- =bx-blee=).
   - Replace each of the 10 =gitCloneBase('<group>', ...)= lines by =gitGroupDir(...)=, with
     =withBase=False= for =bisos-web= and =withDotGithub=False= for =blee-binders=, =bxexamples=, =bxlcnt=.
   - Delete the 9 overview =gitClone= lines.
   - Unchanged: the other =gitClone= lines; the =gitCloneBase= of
     =bisos-pip/bootstrap/dev/bisos/bootstrap-vagrants= (a repo under another name, not a gitGroup);
     =pbdDict_bxReposCollection= (=bxRepos= itself from =ByStar/bxReposBase=, not a gitGroup) and
     =pbdDict_extRepos=; and =gitCloneBase= itself, kept for that one use.
2. *=bxRepos-gitist.pcs=*: two lines in =reposList=. No gitGroup there has a =.github=.

** Decisions needed before 2.2

- *D1. The fto files of the gitGroup directory.* Today =_tree_= (=auxNode=), =_treeProc_=,
  =ftoProc.sh= and =_objectType_= sit in the gitGroup directory because the repo cloned as that
  directory carries them (both =<group>/base= and =bisos-pip/.github= track them). A plain directory has
  none, so an =seedFtoCommon.sh= walk of =/bisos/git/bxRepos= stops at the gitGroup level. Options:
  (a) accept it for now, (b) link them from =base= (=_tree_ -> base/_tree_=, ...), (c) have the
  gitGroup plant create them. Recommended: (a), after checking in 2.2 that nothing in the raw chain
  walks =/bisos/git/bxRepos=; the gitist/fileObj walkers are meant to replace these.
- *D2. Existing platforms (old layout).* Running the new pbd on one (=pltfrmDevelBecome.sh=,
  =bisosBaseDirs.sh -i bxGitReposBasesReClone=): the =directory= step is skipped (it exists); =base=
  and =.github= are cloned *inside* the old clone, as untracked directories (=bisos-pip/base= and
  =blee/base= are already like that here); =bisos-pip/.github= becomes a second clone of the repo the
  directory already is. Recommended: accept it for this stage, and add a separate TODO to migrate an
  existing platform's gitGroup directories to the plain layout.
- *D3. bisos-web and cliGui without base.* Create =bisos-web/base= and =cliGui/base= on GitHub (the
  user's), or leave them baseless for now. Recommended: leave them until they need a plant.

** Decided (2026-11-22)

- D1: the gitGroup directory's fto files will be done differently; deferred.
- D2: no conversion of existing platforms. The target is that a platform is updated by
  re-installing it and re-running its CBMs, so old-layout platforms phase out; this stage makes that
  re-install reliable. An existing platform keeps working, inconsistent with a fresh one; re-running
  the registry on it nests =base= / =.github= clones inside the old clone (harmless, untracked).
  On a fresh install, every gitGroup directory --- =bisos-pip= included --- is a plain directory.
- D3: =bisos-web= and =cliGui= stay without =base=.

** Verification (in 2.2)

- Here, against the editable bisos.common of =dev-bisos3= (no release needed), into a scratch
  =--baseDir=, =--vcMode=anon=: =bx-gitReposBases -i pbdShow --pbdName=bxReposRoot all= (no overview
  key left; each gitGroup's =base=, =.github= and =gitGroup= keys present), then =pbdUpdate= for a subset
  of keys (=blee blee/base blee/.github blee/gitGroup bisos-pip ...=, not =all=: about 120 clones), then
  check =<scratch>/<group>/gitGroup -> .github= and that the three plants resolve under the scratch tree.
- Then bisos.common released (the user's), and a Raw-BISOS run on a VM.
- Only after that: delete the overview repos on GitHub (the user's), and point
  =bisos-pip/base= TODO 6.2, =blee/base= TODO 3.2 and gitist DESIGN.org "Known Problems Now" here.


