*Verified here* (editable bisos.common in =dev-bisos3=, scratch base directory, =--vcMode=anon=):
- The pbd has 187 keys, none with =overview=; each gitGroup has its directory key, then =base=,
  =.github= and =gitGroup= keys as GitHub allows (=bisos-web= without =base=; =blee-binders=,
  =bxexamples=, =bxlcnt= without =.github= and link).
- =bx-gitReposBases -i pbdUpdate= on =bisos-pip=, =blee=, =bxGenesis=, =blee-binders=, =bisos-web=
  (and their member keys), rc 0: each gitGroup directory is a plain directory (no =.git=); =base= and
  =.github= are clones of the right server repos (=blee/base= from =bx-blee/base=); =gitGroup -> .github=.
- A re-run: =git clone= prints "already exists" for =base= and =.github= (as every existing
  =gitClone= does today), the link is unchanged.
- The =blee= plant cloned into the scratch tree resolves its gitGroup there: =gitGroup_members= gives
  =.github= and =base= (the =gitGroup= link is not a member). The =bxGenesis= plant is not on
  GitHub yet (uncommitted), so it was not in the scratch clone.
- No code reaches a file of the old repo-as-directory through the gitGroup path: grep of
  bsip4, bxGenesis, blee and bisos-pip (=*.sh=, =*.py=, =*.cs=, =*.pcs=, =*.spcs=, =*.el=, =*.bash=)
  for =bxRepos/<group>/<top-level file of that repo>=. The only hits are the =This File= comments
